# Keep the deploy to what actually runs in production: app.py, templates/, static/.
#
# This exists because local development now creates several large directories that have
# no business being uploaded. Without it a deploy ships ~400MB of dependencies:
#   desktop/     289MB - Electron binary for the desktop-pet spike
#   venv/         69MB - local Python virtualenv (Vercel installs from requirements.txt)
#   node_modules/ 42MB - three.js + esbuild, only used to build the mascot bundle locally
#
# Note the mascot bundle itself IS deployed when present, because it lives in
# static/vendor/ and is committed as a build artifact -- Vercel runs no Node build step.
node_modules/
desktop/
venv/

# The 2D mascot DOES deploy -- it lives under static/ and is served directly as ES modules
# with no build step. Only its dev harness is excluded.
#
# Note the leading slash matters nowhere here anymore, but it did: an unanchored `mascot/`
# entry (which is what this file used to carry, from when the 3D module lived at the repo
# root) matches a directory of that name at ANY depth, so it would silently exclude
# static/mascot/ and ship a site whose mascot 404s.
static/mascot/dev/

# Local tooling and scratch
.git/
.claude/
*.patch
*.log
server.log
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.DS_Store
.pytest_cache/
